WEBVTT

00:03.270 --> 00:05.850
Well, I like you too.

00:13.280 --> 00:17.070
That's why I can't reciprocate your feelings.

00:21.340 --> 00:22.780
Go home now.

00:22.780 --> 00:23.900
And...

00:23.900 --> 00:27.080
please don't ever come see me again.

00:34.660 --> 00:36.340
Chihiro-senpai...

00:37.940 --> 00:39.010
Yo.

00:39.510 --> 00:41.020
Kei-senpai?!

00:41.670 --> 00:44.690
Love, I've got to feel it

00:44.970 --> 00:48.020
If you put your trust in me

00:48.290 --> 00:51.540
I know what my life would be

00:51.610 --> 00:56.430
Oh, you are all I ever need

00:56.590 --> 01:02.130
I try to hear what you say

01:02.280 --> 01:04.400
So I pray

01:04.480 --> 01:07.980
But you're fading away

01:09.420 --> 01:15.140
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:15.570 --> 01:18.770
We won't fall apart

01:18.890 --> 01:26.950
'Cause you're my only star

01:28.910 --> 01:32.660
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:32.660 --> 01:36.170
Calling you, so like a little child

01:36.330 --> 01:39.410
All the things you have in mind

01:39.670 --> 01:42.790
I wish I could see your insides

01:42.790 --> 01:45.820
My love, you've got to feel it

01:45.820 --> 01:49.130
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:49.340 --> 01:52.790
You know what our lives would be

01:52.910 --> 02:00.750
Oh, you are the one, I believe

02:16.320 --> 02:19.530
Sheesh, you're the worst!

02:19.740 --> 02:22.700
Sometimes I wonder if you're even human!

02:22.700 --> 02:23.950
What do you mean?

02:23.950 --> 02:27.790
Kyosuke, I'm technically your ex-girlfriend, you know.

02:27.790 --> 02:28.710
What about it?

02:29.040 --> 02:32.750
So why are you making me edit videos of your current girlfriend?

02:32.750 --> 02:36.380
Because you're the best at it, of course.

02:38.380 --> 02:40.300
I guess even if you <i>are a failure as a human,</i>

02:40.300 --> 02:43.850
if you capture good footage, then you're a good cameraman.

02:43.850 --> 02:46.470
Is that an insult? Or are you praising me?

02:46.470 --> 02:48.350
Fifty-fifty.

02:48.980 --> 02:50.730
What's that in your hand?

02:51.940 --> 02:54.650
Apparently, it's a good-luck charm for love.

02:54.650 --> 02:56.230
A classmate...

02:56.230 --> 02:57.650
gave it to me.

02:57.650 --> 03:04.160
Tsutsumi's

02:57.650 --> 03:04.160
an idiot!

02:58.070 --> 03:00.530
Well, it's not like <i>I need it or anything.</i>

03:00.530 --> 03:01.820
I take back everything I just said.

03:01.820 --> 03:04.160
You're a failure, seventy-thirty.

03:04.490 --> 03:07.200
Hey, are you satisfied with everything that's going on right now?

03:07.200 --> 03:11.120
In exchange for my editing this,
you'd better help me film <i>my work.</i>

03:11.120 --> 03:14.290
But I'm no longer part of the Film Research Club.

03:14.290 --> 03:17.840
I didn't accept your resignation.

03:17.840 --> 03:19.050
Are you serious?

03:19.050 --> 03:23.050
Do you really think I'd let a talent like yours escape?

03:23.050 --> 03:24.720
Work is work.

03:24.720 --> 03:26.850
Private matters are private matters.

03:26.850 --> 03:29.730
And sex is sex, eh?

03:31.230 --> 03:32.270
How's it going with your girlfriend?

03:32.270 --> 03:33.560
Well...

03:34.060 --> 03:35.980
This really pisses me off.

03:46.620 --> 03:49.500
You can walk on your own two feet now, huh?

03:49.750 --> 03:53.040
Nah, I can't just walk.

03:53.040 --> 03:56.500
As long as I'm able to stand, I'll run as fast as I can!

03:56.500 --> 03:58.960
If you rush that much, won't you trip and fall?

03:58.960 --> 04:02.840
It's fine, because there's someone who will catch me and support me if I fall.

04:04.340 --> 04:07.560
And also, since I have to keep on running.

04:07.850 --> 04:09.850
Because of your sister?

04:10.180 --> 04:14.190
I have to always be a cool sister.

04:14.190 --> 04:18.020
It's important to rest your legs occasionally, you know,

04:18.020 --> 04:19.980
in order to heal your wounds.

04:19.980 --> 04:22.320
Some wounds don't heal.

04:22.320 --> 04:25.700
Are your wounds beyond healing?

04:32.660 --> 04:35.670
Has it already been five years?

04:47.800 --> 04:48.550
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

04:54.980 --> 04:55.730
Sending Email...

04:55.730 --> 04:57.350
Did you eat yet?

04:58.730 --> 04:59.730
Incoming Mail

04:58.730 --> 04:59.730
Chihiro

04:58.730 --> 04:59.730
1 New Mail

04:59.730 --> 05:02.860
Yes, I did. Shrimp and walnut spaghetti.

04:59.730 --> 05:05.650
Did you eat yet?

04:59.900 --> 05:05.650
Yes, I did. Shrimp and walnut spaghetti.

05:02.400 --> 05:05.650
8 points.

05:02.820 --> 05:05.650
What about you, sister?

05:02.860 --> 05:03.900
Eight points.

05:03.900 --> 05:06.700
What about you, sister?

05:06.660 --> 05:10.490
Bento from a convenience store.

05:07.950 --> 05:10.490
4 points...

05:07.990 --> 05:09.120
Four points.

05:09.030 --> 05:10.490
..How are things with Renji-kun?

05:10.490 --> 05:11.240
Message Sent

05:13.250 --> 05:14.000
Incoming Mail

05:13.250 --> 05:14.000
Chihiro

05:13.250 --> 05:14.000
1 New Mail

05:14.000 --> 05:16.830
We're getting along fine.

05:16.750 --> 05:18.750
- I'd like to meet him once.

05:18.750 --> 05:19.500
Message Sent

05:22.250 --> 05:23.010
Incoming Mail

05:22.250 --> 05:23.010
Chihiro

05:22.250 --> 05:23.010
1 New Mail

05:23.010 --> 05:25.840
I want to introduce him to you.

05:23.010 --> 05:26.220
We're getting along fine///

05:23.010 --> 05:26.220
- I'd like to meet him once.

05:27.010 --> 05:30.350
I want to introduce him to you.

05:27.130 --> 05:30.350
I'd like to see you once in a while, too...

05:27.260 --> 05:30.350
I'd like to see you every once in a while, too.

05:30.350 --> 05:31.100
Message Sent

05:32.890 --> 05:33.640
Incoming Mail

05:32.890 --> 05:33.640
Chihiro

05:32.890 --> 05:33.640
1 New Mail

05:33.810 --> 05:36.140
I'd like to see you too.

05:46.860 --> 05:52.540
The city of Otowa in Australia, where Chihiro lives, is supposedly identical to this place.

05:52.540 --> 05:54.660
The only difference is that the seasons are reversed.

05:54.660 --> 05:57.290
The climate is similar to Japan's, and there's no time difference.

05:57.580 --> 06:00.790
Twin cities in different locations.

06:00.790 --> 06:03.800
It's almost like Chihiro and me.

06:03.800 --> 06:07.300
Kei-chan, would you like to see Chihiro-chan?

06:07.300 --> 06:08.130
Yeah.

06:08.800 --> 06:10.140
In that case, why don't you go see her?

06:11.050 --> 06:13.260
Don't make it sound so simple!

06:13.260 --> 06:15.430
She's on the opposite side of the planet, you know!

06:15.430 --> 06:18.060
Isn't Mizuki-chan over there on holiday as well?

06:18.060 --> 06:19.560
Yeah, but...

06:19.560 --> 06:21.980
Then it can't be too hard, can it?

06:21.980 --> 06:23.730
It is too!

06:23.730 --> 06:27.570
Since I don't know how I could face her...

06:27.570 --> 06:30.450
You can decide that when you see her.

06:31.450 --> 06:33.660
Are you still afraid?

06:33.660 --> 06:34.540
Huh?

06:34.540 --> 06:35.830
Of seeing her.

06:35.830 --> 06:37.790
You used to be scared, didn't you?

06:37.790 --> 06:38.960
Yeah...

06:38.960 --> 06:40.710
Even if I'm by your side?

06:41.460 --> 06:44.000
Even though I don't know what the outcome will be,

06:44.000 --> 06:47.210
whatever the outcome is, I'll always be here.

06:47.210 --> 06:49.380
Isn't that enough?

06:50.970 --> 06:51.930
It is.

06:51.930 --> 06:54.680
There! That's how my Kei-chan should be!

06:54.680 --> 06:57.520
Geez, don't treat me like a kid!

06:55.310 --> 06:57.520
Good girl, good girl!

07:00.480 --> 07:04.020
It's all right. I'm not afraid anymore.

07:04.020 --> 07:06.780
Well then, do you want to go see her together?

07:08.400 --> 07:10.280
Nagi-onee-chan!

07:10.280 --> 07:12.780
If two people aren't connected together,

07:12.780 --> 07:15.450
this City Project is meaningless.

07:15.450 --> 07:17.490
Kei-chan, do you have a passport?

07:17.490 --> 07:18.330
Huh?

07:18.330 --> 07:21.330
I'm about to head south as well.

07:21.620 --> 07:23.790
Let's go see Chiro-chan together.

07:24.790 --> 07:26.800
one

07:26.800 --> 07:30.220
Yu-kun... you don't need a sister?

07:32.970 --> 07:36.220
You don't want a sister?

07:36.220 --> 07:39.350
I don't need a sister anymore.

07:40.520 --> 07:42.600
I'm tired of it.

07:43.060 --> 07:44.730
Yu-onii-chan!

07:44.730 --> 07:47.270
Don't call me brother!

07:53.780 --> 07:57.030
I'm still alive.

08:06.500 --> 08:07.670
Yo, Himura.

08:07.670 --> 08:08.670
Morning.

08:08.670 --> 08:10.340
Oh. Morning.

08:10.340 --> 08:13.340
Let me give you a small gift.

08:13.340 --> 08:15.050
Violin Prodigy: Kuze Shuichi-kun's Good Bye party Chapter

08:15.050 --> 08:17.390
Violin Prodigy,

08:17.390 --> 08:20.270
Kuze Shuichi-kun's Goodbye Party Chapter?

08:20.270 --> 08:22.940
Here, I'll give one to you as well, Nagi.

08:22.940 --> 08:23.810
Huh?

08:23.810 --> 08:26.690
I definitely want you guys to come.

08:26.690 --> 08:29.110
Something like a goodbye party doesn't really suit you, does it?

08:29.110 --> 08:31.740
Well, I'll stop by if I have time.

08:31.740 --> 08:34.320
So cold, like always.

08:34.320 --> 08:38.330
Oh yeah, there's also one more person I'd like to invite.

08:38.330 --> 08:41.370
Himura, will you help me invite her?

08:41.370 --> 08:42.450
Me?

08:42.450 --> 08:45.580
I'd like Amamiya Yuko-chan to come as well.

08:46.830 --> 08:48.840
Future,

08:48.840 --> 08:52.300
Have you taken <i>that much of a liking to her?</i>

08:52.300 --> 08:54.510
Not <i>me, but <i>you.</i></i>

08:54.510 --> 08:55.510
Huh?

08:55.510 --> 09:01.010
My instincts tell me that she's truly fit to be my best friend's lover.

09:01.010 --> 09:03.140
Keep your fantasies to yourself.

09:03.140 --> 09:06.190
But you seem to get along well with her.

09:06.400 --> 09:09.110
It's just that she's being overly friendly towards me right now.

09:09.110 --> 09:12.280
That's not how it appears to me, though.

09:12.280 --> 09:13.860
This is pointless.

09:13.860 --> 09:15.990
If you're going to keep it up, I'm going home.

09:17.320 --> 09:20.830
Now, now, don't be so serious.

09:28.080 --> 09:28.960
Yuko?

09:29.250 --> 09:30.540
Oh?

09:30.540 --> 09:33.710
Good morning, Himura-senpai.

09:33.710 --> 09:35.510
What happened, Yuko?

09:35.510 --> 09:38.140
What do you mean, what happened?

09:38.140 --> 09:39.890
Is this the time for fun and games?!

09:39.890 --> 09:41.220
Are you being bullied again?!

09:43.930 --> 09:45.060
This isn't good!

09:45.060 --> 09:45.810
Who is it?!

09:45.810 --> 09:47.310
Who the hell did it?!

09:46.310 --> 09:47.310
Stop it, Himura!

09:47.310 --> 09:48.060
Calm down!

09:50.060 --> 09:53.570
Reawakening memories

09:50.060 --> 09:53.570
Closed up in this chest

10:00.200 --> 10:01.910
Hello, Himura-kun.

10:01.910 --> 10:05.370
Have you finally decided to join the Art Club?

10:05.370 --> 10:08.790
I'm not in the mood for your jokes right now.

10:08.790 --> 10:10.170
Is this about Yuko?

10:10.170 --> 10:11.130
Yes.

10:11.130 --> 10:13.340
I heard it was pretty serious.

10:14.340 --> 10:16.510
You seem unconcerned.

10:16.510 --> 10:19.180
It's really not something to make a fuss about.

10:21.140 --> 10:23.640
I heard that Yuko started it.

10:24.680 --> 10:27.100
That in turn enraged the other girl.

10:27.100 --> 10:30.440
Since she wasn't hurt, I let her go home.

10:30.440 --> 10:32.400
She's probably writing a letter of remorse.

10:32.400 --> 10:33.520
She <i>was hurt.</i>

10:34.570 --> 10:36.610
Yuko was hurt!

10:36.610 --> 10:38.650
There was a wound on her shoulder.

10:38.650 --> 10:40.280
I see.

10:40.280 --> 10:43.530
I wonder why she didn't tell me.

10:43.530 --> 10:48.620
Amamiya-sensei, don't you <i>know that Yuko is being bullied?!</i>

10:48.620 --> 10:49.790
Bullied?

10:49.790 --> 10:50.620
Yes.

10:50.620 --> 10:53.540
It would be a problem if we ignored it, don't you agree?!

10:53.540 --> 10:55.630
Something might happen again.

10:55.630 --> 10:57.130
We have to take action!

11:00.760 --> 11:04.180
Himura-kun, this is a minor issue.

11:05.140 --> 11:07.060
Just ignore it.

11:07.060 --> 11:09.520
This is Yuko's problem.

11:09.520 --> 11:10.980
But...

11:10.980 --> 11:13.650
Don't you feel anything at all?

11:13.650 --> 11:17.400
Even though you're not blood relatives, isn't Yuko your younger sister?

11:17.400 --> 11:20.700
Yes, she's my younger sister.

11:20.700 --> 11:25.410
Accordingly, Himura-kun, an outsider like you shouldn't be interfering in this matter.

11:27.330 --> 11:28.910
Isn't that right?

11:56.940 --> 12:00.780
Didn't you go home?

12:00.780 --> 12:05.120
Isn't there a saying that goes, "In order to deceive your enemy, you must first deceive your ally"?

12:05.120 --> 12:07.830
Who's the enemy, and who's the ally?

12:07.830 --> 12:10.830
Himura-senpai, you're my ally, aren't you?

12:11.580 --> 12:13.330
Who knows?

12:14.210 --> 12:15.710
But you're so kind.

12:16.460 --> 12:18.750
Quit talking nonsense!

12:20.340 --> 12:22.050
Did you go to the infirmary?

12:22.050 --> 12:22.880
Huh?

12:22.880 --> 12:24.180
You were hurt, weren't you?

12:24.180 --> 12:25.970
Did you get treatment?

12:25.970 --> 12:28.720
See? Just as I thought.

12:28.720 --> 12:33.190
Just as I thought, you're my kind ally, Himura-senpai.

12:33.190 --> 12:35.730
I told you, it's nothing like that!

12:39.650 --> 12:43.030
I thought you were just going to let them be.

12:43.030 --> 12:47.490
Didn't you say that you'd smile and pretend you weren't hurt, even if something bad happened?

12:48.330 --> 12:51.500
It's unlike you to get into a fight.

12:51.500 --> 12:53.000
That's true.

12:53.000 --> 12:56.540
I just thought that a new reaction might entertain them.

12:56.540 --> 12:57.880
Seriously...

12:58.130 --> 13:03.880
To tell you the truth, that was my first time hitting someone.

13:04.630 --> 13:07.640
It's actually pretty painful, isn't it?

13:07.640 --> 13:09.640
What in the world happened?

13:09.640 --> 13:13.980
A classmate was going through my bag.

13:13.980 --> 13:15.190
Your bag?

13:15.190 --> 13:18.860
And when I saw that, I suddenly got really angry.

13:18.860 --> 13:20.150
I see.

13:20.150 --> 13:21.530
I'm sorry.

13:22.530 --> 13:25.650
I'm sorry, Himura-senpai.

13:25.650 --> 13:27.820
Why are you apologizing to <i>me?</i>

13:27.820 --> 13:30.870
Of course I'm going to apologize.

13:30.870 --> 13:32.160
Because...

13:32.160 --> 13:35.160
I made the person I like worry.

13:35.660 --> 13:37.080
Why?

13:37.080 --> 13:37.750
Yes?

13:37.750 --> 13:40.710
It's only been a few days since our reunion.

13:40.710 --> 13:44.510
And yet, how can you say something like that?

13:44.510 --> 13:46.840
I've always imagined...

13:46.840 --> 13:48.140
Imagined?

13:48.140 --> 13:51.810
...what kind of person Yu-kun had become.

13:53.640 --> 13:58.600
At the orphanage, where everyone was grieving over the deaths of their relatives,

13:58.600 --> 14:01.150
the one boy who was fiercely alive...

14:01.480 --> 14:05.940
the boy who loved to draw, and who was always looking ahead...

14:05.940 --> 14:09.200
I wondered what kind of man he grew up to be.

14:10.280 --> 14:15.200
It turned out that he grew up to be exactly what I imagined.

14:16.250 --> 14:19.210
What did you imagine I'd grow up to be?

14:19.210 --> 14:20.460
That is...

14:20.460 --> 14:21.590
a secret.

14:52.490 --> 14:58.000
I wonder if I should hold a farewell party before the ticking stops?

14:59.750 --> 15:02.500
I guess that's no longer a good idea.

15:04.800 --> 15:09.130
This place really <i>is identical to the Otowa in Japan, isn't it?</i>

15:09.130 --> 15:13.140
Yes! I was also quite shocked when I first saw it.

15:13.140 --> 15:16.010
It's winter over there, but it's so hot here.

15:16.010 --> 15:18.020
It's really amazing, isn't it?

15:18.020 --> 15:22.980
But to me, it's more amazing that I got to see you!

15:22.980 --> 15:24.440
This is like a miracle!

15:24.440 --> 15:27.280
I wasn't planning on coming here, either.

15:27.280 --> 15:31.660
I'm really low on senpai energy right now.

15:31.660 --> 15:33.490
Please let me recharge!

15:33.490 --> 15:37.040
Geez, it's already so hot.

15:37.040 --> 15:38.410
Mizuki?

15:38.410 --> 15:39.960
What is it?

15:39.960 --> 15:41.830
Did something happen?

15:41.830 --> 15:43.460
Yes.

15:43.460 --> 15:45.340
Should I ask?

15:45.340 --> 15:47.670
I might want you to.

15:47.670 --> 15:50.090
You always overexert yourself.

15:50.090 --> 15:52.550
I learned that from you.

15:52.550 --> 15:55.010
<i>I never push myself too hard.</i>

15:55.010 --> 15:58.850
If you say that, it's proof that you're someone who pushes herself too hard.

15:58.850 --> 16:01.480
I can't win.

16:01.770 --> 16:06.270
Kei-senpai, why did you suddenly decide to come here?

16:06.270 --> 16:09.990
I've got some homework to do.

16:09.990 --> 16:11.240
Homework?

16:11.240 --> 16:12.490
Yeah.

16:12.490 --> 16:14.740
Homework that I've let pile up for five years.

16:15.740 --> 16:18.290
Kei... onee-chan?

16:22.870 --> 16:24.040
Chihiro?

16:35.470 --> 16:36.550
Onee-chan!

16:36.550 --> 16:37.800
Chihiro!

16:39.810 --> 16:41.680
I wanted to see you.

16:41.680 --> 16:44.230
I wanted to see you, too!

16:44.230 --> 16:51.230
There were things that I had to tell you when we met in person.

16:52.280 --> 16:55.240
It's all right. It's okay.

16:55.240 --> 17:01.240
I... remember what happened before the accident, as if it were yesterday.

17:01.240 --> 17:03.750
It's all right. It's fine now.

17:03.750 --> 17:06.250
I'm sorry, onee-chan!

17:08.250 --> 17:10.920
There's no reason for you to apologize.

17:10.920 --> 17:14.260
Because I'm the one who really needs to apologize!

17:14.260 --> 17:18.640
It's because I was at fault. That's why I was punished.

17:19.140 --> 17:23.980
Even though I knew you liked Hiro-onii-chan as well!

17:23.980 --> 17:26.650
It's because I was keeping him to myself.

17:26.650 --> 17:29.900
That's not it. That's really not it!

17:29.900 --> 17:32.190
That's why it turned out like this!

17:32.190 --> 17:34.900
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry!

17:34.900 --> 17:37.910
That's not it...

17:40.950 --> 17:42.450
When they're together,

17:42.450 --> 17:47.170
they both blame themselves like that, ultimately hurting each other.

17:47.920 --> 17:53.170
When you think of another's feelings and blame yourself, it actually makes the other suffer more.

17:53.170 --> 17:57.880
Even if their hearts connect and they forgive each other, as soon as Chiro-chan loses her memories,

17:57.880 --> 18:01.140
the cycle will start again and damage them further.

18:01.140 --> 18:03.720
It goes on and on, repeating itself.

18:03.720 --> 18:07.440
That's why they had to be separated.

18:08.190 --> 18:11.820
But it looks like we don't have to worry about that anymore.

18:21.160 --> 18:25.450
A lot has happened to you as well?

18:25.450 --> 18:26.250
Yeah.

18:26.250 --> 18:31.540
Thanks to Tsutsumi-senpai, I summoned my courage and decided to come see you like this.

18:31.540 --> 18:34.210
I'll introduce you to him in the future.

18:34.210 --> 18:35.210
Okay!

18:35.210 --> 18:39.880
Chihiro, you've gone through a lot too, haven't you?

18:39.880 --> 18:45.770
Thanks to Renji-kun, I'm not sad anymore.

18:48.100 --> 18:49.980
You've become strong, haven't you?

18:49.980 --> 18:52.860
Because I want to be like you!

18:53.610 --> 18:59.240
I, too, sometimes wish that I was just like you, Chihiro.

18:59.240 --> 19:07.120
In the end, both you and I became involved with someone other than Hiro-onii-san?

19:07.120 --> 19:08.500
You're right.

19:11.210 --> 19:13.920
Chihiro, are you happy now?

19:13.920 --> 19:16.000
Yes. What about you?

19:16.000 --> 19:17.130
Of course!

19:18.720 --> 19:22.300
I'm glad I came! I got to see your smile.

19:22.300 --> 19:23.800
Me too.

19:24.890 --> 19:30.140
The two of them can finally walk on their own feet now.

19:31.390 --> 19:37.150
And with this, no matter what happens,
they'll be able to stand up on their own.

19:38.150 --> 19:41.650
There's nothing to worry about now.

19:41.910 --> 19:44.120
What can I do...

19:44.120 --> 19:47.160
What can I do to be like them?

19:48.660 --> 19:53.210
In order not to hurt the person that I like, I end up hurting myself.

19:53.210 --> 19:56.420
And that in turn hurts him more.

19:59.460 --> 20:03.840
I try to distance myself from him, for his benefit.

20:03.840 --> 20:07.850
And that rebounds and makes him suffer even more!

20:07.850 --> 20:09.430
What can I do...

20:09.430 --> 20:12.940
What can I do to stop this sad cycle?

20:12.940 --> 20:14.440
What can I do?

20:14.440 --> 20:16.440
Are you perhaps...

20:17.190 --> 20:19.940
I see, so you're that girl.

20:19.940 --> 20:20.690
Huh?

20:20.690 --> 20:24.860
I heard that you've been following Kuze around.

20:24.860 --> 20:28.200
Would you stop that? You're a nuisance.

20:28.200 --> 20:29.450
But...

20:29.450 --> 20:30.540
why?!

20:31.540 --> 20:34.790
Because I'm going out with Kuze Shuichi.

20:50.470 --> 21:03.860
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

21:04.450 --> 21:11.290
The echoing sounds sparkle.

21:11.410 --> 21:14.790
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

21:15.040 --> 21:22.420
I should be able to find it again

21:24.720 --> 21:27.590
Holding firmly onto your sound,

21:28.220 --> 21:37.770
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

21:38.730 --> 21:44.570
Please don't forget the important things.

21:45.740 --> 21:52.240
A smile continues on into the future.

22:07.720 --> 22:10.510
Do you have a moment, Yuko?

22:10.510 --> 22:11.760
Nii-san.

22:11.760 --> 22:14.470
What happened today?

22:14.470 --> 22:18.690
A classmate was going through my bag.

22:18.690 --> 22:19.850
Bag?

22:19.850 --> 22:22.730
<i>That's inside it.</i>

22:22.730 --> 22:24.480
I see.

22:24.480 --> 22:27.780
Well, I won't ask anymore.

22:28.780 --> 22:31.870
I've got my own viewpoint as well.

22:31.870 --> 22:34.790
Do you really care about those things?

22:34.790 --> 22:37.370
Heh, you have a point.

22:37.750 --> 22:40.790
Did you show him your arm?

22:40.790 --> 22:41.920
No.

22:41.920 --> 22:43.710
I'll say this clearly.

22:43.710 --> 22:48.130
The thing he fears most is abandoning you.

22:49.260 --> 22:50.760
How foolish,

22:50.760 --> 22:54.890
when he should be focusing solely on saving himself.

22:54.890 --> 22:58.390
It's impossible to repent your sins against the dead.

22:58.730 --> 23:01.100
To think that you carried it around with you...

23:01.100 --> 23:04.230
You're the one who gave it to me as a protective charm, right?

23:04.230 --> 23:05.980
What are you planning to do?

23:05.980 --> 23:07.780
Nothing.

23:07.780 --> 23:09.860
I just want to see how this turns out.

23:09.860 --> 23:13.530
That is how humans choose the wrong path.

23:13.910 --> 23:18.040
I chose the wrong path a long time ago.

23:18.040 --> 23:19.290
I see.

23:19.290 --> 23:20.540
You're right.

23:26.050 --> 23:30.840
Feelings that reached their target, and feelings that did not.

23:30.840 --> 23:34.050
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:34.050 --> 23:35.810
Flection.

23:35.810 --> 23:38.930
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
